1
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:10,276
It is three in the morning in a house in Manila. Everyone is asleep... except one person.

2
00:00:10,676 --> 00:00:13,280
She whispers, "Just one more episode."

3
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:15,921
She has said this six times tonight.

4
00:00:16,321 --> 00:00:24,579
Across the Philippines, millions of people know exactly how she feels. So why are Filipinos so in love with Korean dramas?

5
00:00:25,879 --> 00:00:32,707
Our story begins in two thousand three, when the network G M A aired a Korean show called Bright Girl.

6
00:00:33,107 --> 00:00:39,828
Korean dramas were dubbed into Filipino, so lolas, titos and kids could all follow every word.

7
00:00:40,228 --> 00:00:50,320
That same year, Endless Love: Autumn in My Heart became a huge hit, and viewers cried so much it was shown again in two thousand four and two thousand six.

8
00:00:50,720 --> 00:00:56,460
Then came Lovers in Paris, and suddenly everyone was shouting the Korean cheer: "Aja!"

9
00:00:57,760 --> 00:01:01,047
So what makes these stories so hard to stop watching?

10
00:01:01,447 --> 00:01:06,483
First, they are short. Many K-dramas finish in about sixteen episodes.

11
00:01:06,883 --> 00:01:16,463
A Filipino teleserye can run for months, sometimes years. A K-drama says hello, breaks your heart, and says goodbye in about two months.

12
00:01:16,863 --> 00:01:24,224
Second, the stories feel familiar: big families, kind grandmothers, strict parents, and lots and lots of food.

13
00:01:25,524 --> 00:01:30,347
A Korean family and a Filipino family turn out to be almost twins.

14
00:01:30,747 --> 00:01:36,188
In both, you respect your elders, you eat together, and you are always asked, "Have you eaten?"

15
00:01:36,588 --> 00:01:44,888
In a Filipino home, a younger person adds "po" to be polite. In a Korean drama, younger characters use polite words too.

16
00:01:46,188 --> 00:01:48,088
And then there is the romance.

17
00:01:48,488 --> 00:01:56,084
Slow walks in the snow, piggyback rides, and that one moment where someone catches someone who trips... in slow motion.

18
00:01:56,484 --> 00:02:01,093
Viewers scream, hug their pillows, and reach for the tissue box. Again.

19
00:02:02,393 --> 00:02:09,349
In two thousand nine, the Korean show Boys Over Flowers arrived, and the country went flower-boy crazy.

20
00:02:09,749 --> 00:02:17,580
Filipino networks even made their own versions of Korean hits, like My Love from the Star in two thousand seventeen.

21
00:02:18,880 --> 00:02:22,977
Then the dramas moved from the living room to the palm of your hand.

22
00:02:23,377 --> 00:02:29,757
In two thousand twenty, people stayed home during the pandemic, and K-drama watching exploded.

23
00:02:30,157 --> 00:02:36,473
On Netflix, K-drama viewing in the Philippines jumped more than three hundred fifty percent that year.

24
00:02:36,873 --> 00:02:44,917
And Crash Landing on You, about a South Korean heiress who paraglides into North Korea, became the country's most searched show.

25
00:02:46,217 --> 00:02:48,331
Researchers have studied this too.

26
00:02:48,731 --> 00:02:59,057
In one Philippine study of two hundred university students, the top reasons were exciting plots, fast stories, attractive characters, and great music.

27
00:02:59,457 --> 00:03:10,616
And in a Korean government survey released in twenty twenty-five, the Philippines showed the most love for Korean culture, with about eighty-nine percent of fans viewing it favorably.

28
00:03:11,916 --> 00:03:14,520
But maybe the biggest reason is simple.

29
00:03:14,920 --> 00:03:17,503
A K-drama is something you can share.

30
00:03:17,903 --> 00:03:24,965
Mothers and daughters watch together. Friends text each other, "Have you reached episode ten? Don't tell me anything!"

31
00:03:25,365 --> 00:03:30,615
Even the grumpiest tito pretends not to watch, but he knows every character's name.

32
00:03:31,915 --> 00:03:34,412
Back in Manila, the sun is coming up.

33
00:03:34,812 --> 00:03:42,707
The episode ends. She sighs, smiles, and reaches for the tissue box... and finds the whole family already sharing it.

34
00:03:43,107 --> 00:03:47,716
Because in the Philippines, the best love story is the one you watch together.
